WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.530
- [Narrator] Orbiting the Earth
at 17,500 miles per hour...

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.580
- [Speaker] Oh, there it went.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.840
- [Narrator] Is the Space Station.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.290
Or, I'm sorry: The
International Space Station,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.000
because there's two now.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.060
The international one used
by the US, Russia, Europe,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.830
Canada, Japan, and others;

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.800
and China's Tiangong, which
became fully operational

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.780
at the end of 2022.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.350
They plan to use it for at
least the next 10 to 15 years.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.450
Meanwhile, the International Space Station

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.280
is set to be retired before that.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.320
- International Space
Station is going down.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.610
Chinese space station is going up.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.020
I won't say it's a changing of the guard,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.180
but does indicate that
things are changing.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.670
The people who are up
in space are changing.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.950
The evolution of use of space is changing.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.230
- [Narrator] Chinese and US
astronauts aren't allowed

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.970
on their opposing space stations.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:48.060
They are effectively banned
from directly working together

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.660
because of one small
section in a 2011 law.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.080
Here's why the US and China
don't work together in space,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.743
and why that law is now a big
debate in the space community.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.000
Leading up to the amendment,
there was a lot of tension

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.800
between the US and China.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.630
There were numerous cyber attacks,

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.310
including on members of Congress.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.930
- On these computers was information

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.490
about all the case work I've done

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.900
on behalf of political dissonance

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.930
and human rights activists
around the world.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.940
- [Narrator] In 2007, China completed

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.470
a ballistic missile test,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.660
creating a tremendous amount of debris

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.000
when it destroyed a weather satellite;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.130
debris the International Space Station

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.740
still has to maneuver around.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.030
In news stories at the time,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.700
the concern wasn't
immediately the station,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.280
but the showing of China's military might.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.980
- Space is a key national
security enabler.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.170
- [Narrator] Victoria Samson
works for an organization

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.840
that promotes global cooperation in space.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:43.860
Her career has focused

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.860
on that intersection between
space and the military.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.350
- There's kind of a natural correlation

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.780
between a ballistic missile program

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.070
and a satellite launch program.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.410
That was only the third country
to do that sort of thing.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.240
The US and the Soviet Union had done them

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.540
during the Cold War, but there
hadn't been one officially

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.950
for decades at that point.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.840
I think that was really kind of a reminder

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.840
that there are new actors
in space and new interests,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.640
and so the United States needed to think

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.250
about how it wants to deal with space.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.310
- [Narrator] Then, in 2010,
the head of NASA went to China

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.920
to begin talks of collaborating together,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.830
possibly even on the
International Space Station.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.990
As he described it in 2021...

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.020
- Before I went, met with Congressman Wolf

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.010
because he was the chairman

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.750
of the House Appropriations Committee

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.870
responsible for NASA funding,
and he asked me not to go.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.580
In fact, he told me not to go.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.530
- [Narrator] He's talking
about that Congressman,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.410
Frank Wolf, who was
passionate about investigating

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.780
and punishing China's human rights abuses,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.300
and felt that even
normalizing trade with China

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.320
in the 90s was...

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.430
- Fundamentally immoral,
and this Congress is ready

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.150
to ratify a fundamentally immoral policy,

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.410
a policy that has no morality behind it.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.480
- [Narrator] In 2011, he added a clause

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.450
to that NASA funding bill
that says the space agency

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.280
can't participate, collaborate,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.370
or coordinate bilaterally
in any way with China

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.440
or any Chinese-owned companies,

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.600
unless it's approved by Congress.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.550
It's called the Wolf Amendment.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.750
It's not a total ban,

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.240
but it's created what
many call speed bumps,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.850
which functionally serve
to ban collaboration.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:20.880
- The Wolf Amendment does
not prevent the United States

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.280
from doing things with
China on space issues,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.860
but it does send a message
that the United States

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.470
is leery about working
with China on space issues.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.150
- [Narrator] The US has long used space

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.100
as kind of a soft power.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.430
The US-Russia relationship
was a key example of that,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.860
working together on
compatible docking systems

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.240
despite the Cold War,

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.280
and then, of course, the Space Station.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.570
- The International Space Station

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.360
has been a very effective
tool for diplomatic outreach.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.430
But, you know, the United
States wasn't reaching out

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.050
to other countries out of the
goodness of their own heart,

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.120
and it felt that there were benefits

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.240
that the program could get
from the various partners.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.980
The Russians had, you know, experience

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.960
under the Soviet Union of
having their own space stations.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.180
They would bring that tactical expertise.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.830
- [Narrator] China originally wasn't part

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.300
of the International Space Station,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.640
because they just didn't
have the technical knowledge

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.570
at the time.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.910
This is the total amount
of launches conducted

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.860
by the US and Russia,

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.240
and here's China.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.210
In 2011, while their space
program had improved,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.430
they were still far behind,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.590
or as Congressman Wolf said at the time,

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.930
he didn't want to give
China the opportunity

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.060
to take advantage of our technology,

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.850
and we have nothing to gain
from dealing with them.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.021
But a decade later, things have changed.

00:04:29.021 --> 00:04:31.950
(rocket roaring)
(person speaking indistinctly)

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.340
China has been quickly stepping
up how often it launches,

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.380
and the future plans of both countries

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.110
will be in the same place: the Moon.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.740
NASA says they plan to have
a crewed mission in 2025,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.440
look to establish a longer
term presence there,

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.970
and in the years ahead,

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.640
establish another
multinational space station,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.520
the Lunar Gateway, that
will orbit the moon.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.560
China says they also plan to have a camp

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.590
on the same part of the moon by 2028.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.040
But if these two base camps
wanna coordinate or collaborate,

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.010
they need to go to Congress
30 days in advance.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:05.910
- Particularly when you're looking

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.790
at such a hostile
environment such as the Moon,

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:13.200
it seems foolish to needlessly
complicate relationships

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.870
and create a hostile working environment

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.280
with one of the only other countries

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.370
that perhaps could help out
human beings on the moon,

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.070
just because you have hostile
relationships on the ground.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.090
- [Narrator] That's why there's a debate

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.230
in the space community

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:28.200
about whether this law should
exist in its current form.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.020
- If you look at what was
Congressman Frank Wolf's purpose,

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.180
which was to try to isolate the Chinese

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.980
and to, more closely,
abiding with our norms

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:42.813
in human rights, it did not
accomplish its purpose at all.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.700
If we're looking at slowing
their program or keeping them

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.480
from developing a space program,
it did not do that at all.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.850
Unfortunately, what it
has done has caused us

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.040
to now be on the outside looking in,

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.700
as China presses forward with
their 50 year space program

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.830
and doing things that some people say

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.690
they're moving at an incredible pace.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.760
- [Narrator] Congressman
Wolf, who is now retired,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.410
told the Wall Street
Journal in a statement

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.900
that if a planned
collaboration doesn't meet

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.790
the amendment's basic criteria,

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.160
NASA has no business doing it,

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.490
and referred to China's
continuing human rights abuses.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.410
- I think the Wolf
Amendment is gonna be around

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.890
for a while, partially
because no one wants

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.830
to spend the political
capital to get rid of it,

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:28.170
partially because I think
the pendulum has really swung

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:33.170
in terms of concerns about
China as a rival or threat.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:36.900
- They could go to the
South Pole of the Moon

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.650
where the resources are,
and they could land,

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.650
and they would say, "This
is our exclusive territory.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.907
You stay out."

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.473
And we're not gonna let that happen.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.870
- [Narrator] The Wolf
Amendment has been kept

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.870
in each NASA funding
bill since its creation,

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:58.050
but as the US and China both
move closer to the Moon,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.780
the space community's
debate over collaboration

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.813
may become a congressional one.

00:07:02.813 --> 00:07:05.563
(relaxing music)

